{"title":"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> of real numbers which satisfy the simultaneous equations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b12fab9ef3a6492d388b54f987b1c39ef2f62a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = y^3 + y - 8\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51d6db5134e940dee508c425fd10149e2002e50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = z^3 + z - 8\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271f22a292eb80b397d9cf0c81ce8b96602adc47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z = x^3 + x - 8.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To start, since all three equations have a similar form, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b0046a7446d1f3047baf2c28fd25355f57ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" /> to see if there are any solutions.  Doing so results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d083e7e289eb44a23bd63a05f2fc166092058b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x &amp;= x^3 + x - 8 \\\\ 0 &amp;= x^3 - 8 \\\\ 0 &amp;= (x-2)(x^2 + 2x + 4). \\end{align*}\" width=\"198\" height=\"75\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7c7b4dcab3dc0b8a38ec78e0824dab735a6137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 2x + 4 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> has complex solutions, so the solution where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b0046a7446d1f3047baf2c28fd25355f57ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4d0787f258358551930ba1f3dbdab59fa1a9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAdditionally, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are monotonically increasing functions, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce8e5540cf6d09c36c8425e3daa49e7312e937f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + x - 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> is a monotonically increasing function.  Thus, we can suspect that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4d0787f258358551930ba1f3dbdab59fa1a9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is the only solution.  To prove this, we can use proof by contradiction.\n</p><p><br />\nAssume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac460617bfc48fea8747c0f19e1eced57ae4a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is a monotonically increasing function, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/103390e21005b0df1b31e61780071a4947afe68e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68cff39a5528b36fd2c7a7ff5db82910b0270c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 8 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dd1ee072a2fbce1f052009695a9af0179a499b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + x - 8 &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502032ec96175710bacc2492aaac6371ec6ea6bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.  By doing the same steps, we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67187628808888fc3fd57453009875bb127fb6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z &gt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8987614aeb29fca9d2c3a5c927bbe3b24f9c21b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />.  However, that would mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30ce9093d520dd8e1c7b2b6842ca0e4fbd815857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" />, which does not work, so there are no solutions where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac460617bfc48fea8747c0f19e1eced57ae4a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSimilarly, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84958f805b063032d2629160e880abc1487afa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is a monotonically increasing function, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c510c9c9640b99f810eee68e27ca09041e4574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 &lt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425bbb7473eaef1172e645d84de9f68183eb1c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 8 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d68a2305d2c875ee8d198cc03ed300e6471fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + x - 8 &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f076982698ce1daa37e489864888cf32e94d1d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.  By doing the same steps, we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e870e2e40dd67794242e1b00bdb1a000fdc52c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z &lt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622a41a9a56bcbba1dc8b9fe70292bdcfdfc5257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />.  However, that would mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/992ec582beade636c44dc102f418f25fb5f19294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" />, which does not work, so there are no solutions where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84958f805b063032d2629160e880abc1487afa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we proved that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is the only solution, and by substituting the value into the original equations, we get the only solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26c1b1e2b18c3e02226ce76a2cc79c9c97366d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(2,2,2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"69\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO\">2007 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213816\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 213/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1044/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6216/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.364      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    7.364      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18260:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213816 and revision id 119769. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}